    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm looking at some ceramic fragments from a new trench in the southern sector and im having trouble distinguishing between the late helladic iii and early geometric stuff. how can i tell the difference just by looking at the firing and the surface treatment?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Look closely at the slip and surface finish; Late Helladic III wares often exhibit a more burnished, often reddish-brown finish, while Early Geometric pieces commonly show a thicker, lighter slip. Examine the fabric color as well, as LH III generally has a more vitrified body compared to the sometimes grittier texture of early Geometric ceramics. If there are any painted decoration elements, the transition to complex, figurative imagery will clearly mark the shift to the Geometric.",
      "source": "target",
